<h2>&lt;BbScanner&gt; methods and properties</h2>
<pre><code>Task            StartAsync(string? deviceId = null)
Task            StopAsync()
void            Pause()
void            Resume()
Task            SwitchCameraAsync(string deviceId)
Task&lt;bool&gt;      SetTorchAsync(bool on)
Task&lt;bool&gt;      SetZoomAsync(double zoom)
Task            OpenFilePickerAsync()
Task&lt;IReadOnlyList&lt;BbCameraDevice&gt;&gt; GetCamerasAsync()
BbBarcodeResult?  DecodeImage(ReadOnlySpan&lt;byte&gt; pixels, int width, int height, BbPixelFormat format)

BbScannerStatus   Status
BbCameraInfo?     Camera
IReadOnlyList&lt;BbCameraDevice&gt; Cameras
BbScanDiagnostics Diagnostics
long            FramesDecoded
long            FramesWithSymbol
bool            IsTorchOn
double          Zoom
(int, int)      ProcessingSize</code></pre>

<p class="field__hint">
    <code>StartAsync</code> is safe to call at any time: a call that arrives while an earlier one
    is still waiting for the permission prompt supersedes it, and the superseded request releases
    its camera rather than leaving it running. The same holds for <code>StopAsync</code> and for
    disposal, so navigating away mid-prompt never leaves the camera indicator lit.
</p>

